NextBSD local patch for vendored Apple libxml2-39.10 (libxml2 2.9.13 based)

CVE:      none assigned (heap use-after-free in xmlRelaxNGValidateValue when
          a deferred XML_RELAXNG_ERR_LISTEXTRA error keeps a pointer into a
          freed list value; libxml2 issue #1055, MR !382)
Upstream: df2ba65f661addfba50bdb7f280d594781249dfc (v2.15.2)
          5dfd9065ec30d3fe19998cd270b5a9dec0125ed1 (master)
          "use duplicating variant in relaxng to mitigate UAF"
Adapted:  Verbatim one-line change (VALID_ERR2 -> VALID_ERR2P, which
          duplicates the string), context offsets only.

diff --git a/relaxng.c b/relaxng.c
--- a/relaxng.c
+++ b/relaxng.c
@@ -8930,7 +8930,7 @@ xmlRelaxNGValidateValue(xmlRelaxNGValidCtxtPtr ctxt,
 
                 if ((ret == 0) && (ctxt->state->value != NULL) &&
                     (ctxt->state->value != ctxt->state->endvalue)) {
-                    VALID_ERR2(XML_RELAXNG_ERR_LISTEXTRA,
+                    VALID_ERR2P(XML_RELAXNG_ERR_LISTEXTRA,
                                ctxt->state->value);
                     ret = -1;
                 }
